WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.296
Since January 2026, the connected
V16 beacon is mandatory in Spain.

2
00:00:06.646 --> 00:00:10.998
Switch it on and it sends your
position to the DGT 3.0 platform.

3
00:00:11.348 --> 00:00:14.313
Traffic forwards it to
connected navigation apps.

4
00:00:14.663 --> 00:00:17.714
It is a big step. But a light
does not know what happened.

5
00:00:18.064 --> 00:00:21.499
It doesn't know if it was a crash,
your lane, or which way you face.

6
00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:24.494
And if nobody can switch
it on, it warns no one.

7
00:00:26.094 --> 00:00:27.438
This is SENDA Drive.

8
00:00:27.788 --> 00:00:31.671
The engine that turns the beacon into
information for whoever comes behind.

9
00:00:32.021 --> 00:00:35.242
It lives in your phone, understands
the road and invents nothing.

10
00:00:36.842 --> 00:00:39.445
You authorise it once and pair your car.

11
00:00:39.795 --> 00:00:43.528
Get in, and the car's Bluetooth
starts it; get out, and it closes.

12
00:00:43.878 --> 00:00:47.505
If there is only a weak hint, it
waits for speed to confirm it.

13
00:00:47.855 --> 00:00:49.967
Without your permission, it never starts.

14
00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:53.581
Android, with or without Google,
and iPhone share the same logic,

15
00:00:53.931 --> 00:00:57.792
checked against 10 shared
scenarios and 55 steps.

16
00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:03.189
Fog, 120 km/h, 1.2 seconds between cars.

17
00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:06.569
Each driver reacts to
the brake lights ahead.

18
00:01:06.919 --> 00:01:10.268
The delays add up: in the
model, five cars crash.

19
00:01:10.618 --> 00:01:14.714
With SENDA, the first phone detects
the braking and warns everyone at once.

20
00:01:15.064 --> 00:01:19.395
In the model only the tailgater
crashes. Only distance fixes that.

21
00:01:19.745 --> 00:01:23.222
With no coverage, the SOS
rides with passing cars:

22
00:01:23.572 --> 00:01:28.031
out in about seven minutes with
one car in ten. It is a simulation.

23
00:01:29.631 --> 00:01:34.132
A real case, told by one of the
drivers. Anonymous and unverified.

24
00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:38.983
A Belgian motorway. A truck's
cab strikes the side of a car.

25
00:01:39.333 --> 00:01:43.067
It drags it sideways, lets go,
and the car spins half a turn.

26
00:01:43.417 --> 00:01:46.787
It stops in the fast
lane, facing the traffic.

27
00:01:47.137 --> 00:01:51.404
The truck, on the shoulder. The
real danger comes now: those behind.

28
00:01:53.004 --> 00:01:56.503
This case exposed a bug in our own code.

29
00:01:56.853 --> 00:02:01.034
Because the car faced backwards, the
warning was dropped: 'other direction'.

30
00:02:01.384 --> 00:02:05.565
Everyone arriving behind would
have ignored it. It is fixed.

31
00:02:05.915 --> 00:02:09.990
Now, with no reliable heading, it warns
and flags the road side as uncertain.

32
00:02:10.340 --> 00:02:13.348
If the phone sends the heading
it had before the impact,

33
00:02:13.698 --> 00:02:16.941
the opposite carriageway no
longer gets a false alarm.

34
00:02:18.541 --> 00:02:21.741
In the app, with no sign-up:
what to do now, step by step.

35
00:02:22.091 --> 00:02:26.421
A button to call 112, always yours:
SENDA never calls on its own.

36
00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:30.761
A script for the call, with lane and
direction only if you declare them.

37
00:02:31.111 --> 00:02:35.015
And warnings fused from several
sources, each with its provenance.

38
00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:40.369
The phone feels the impact too: the
accelerometer measures the jolt,

39
00:02:40.719 --> 00:02:44.815
and the gyroscope, how far the car turns
afterwards. That spin was the clue.

40
00:02:45.165 --> 00:02:48.728
Each signal adds or removes
evidence; none decides alone.

41
00:02:49.078 --> 00:02:53.025
Today's weights are examples, and the
spin weight stays empty until calibrated.

42
00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:57.300
The calibration harness is ready:
it trains and tests separately.

43
00:02:58.900 --> 00:03:03.167
Many cars carry cameras. Their owner
can run the clips through SENDA.

44
00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:07.783
It spots a car sideways, one stopped
ahead, or a person on the road.

45
00:03:08.133 --> 00:03:11.611
And it only shares the event: what,
where and when. Never the image.

46
00:03:11.961 --> 00:03:15.246
If an event carries an image, a
plate or a face, it is rejected.

47
00:03:15.596 --> 00:03:19.841
What a Tesla's computer sees is not
open to third parties. We don't pretend.

48
00:03:20.191 --> 00:03:24.309
Until calibrated, cameras do not raise
confidence: they are only logged.

49
00:03:25.909 --> 00:03:29.855
For the traffic centre, a map of
the incident with its provenance.

50
00:03:30.205 --> 00:03:33.363
Sources that copy each
other count only once.

51
00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:37.681
And a lab to replay every
case, marked as an exercise.

52
00:03:39.281 --> 00:03:43.057
Android in two versions: one with
no Google services and no Internet,

53
00:03:43.407 --> 00:03:46.159
and one with Google and
an Android Auto screen.

54
00:03:46.509 --> 00:03:50.967
Android Auto only allows certain
categories: ours is still provisional.

55
00:03:51.317 --> 00:03:55.051
And a new iPhone app, built
and tested on every change.

56
00:03:56.651 --> 00:04:00.896
Every change is checked: 881 core tests,

57
00:04:01.246 --> 00:04:05.406
82 checks of the road
app in a real browser,

58
00:04:05.756 --> 00:04:10.705
and 55 automatic-start steps,
identical on every platform.

59
00:04:11.055 --> 00:04:14.298
What is missing, we say:
there are no field trials yet,

60
00:04:14.648 --> 00:04:17.891
automatic start has not
been tested on real phones,

61
00:04:18.241 --> 00:04:21.462
and the detectors are not
calibrated with real data.

62
00:04:21.812 --> 00:04:24.756
Next step: a pilot with real drivers.

63
00:04:26.356 --> 00:04:29.492
SENDA Drive. So that whoever
comes behind knows in time.

64
00:04:29.842 --> 00:04:32.765
Open source, at the address on screen.
